---

# Key phase boundaries

## 1. API layer

Current `mod.ts` already mixes parsing, import resolution, checking, artifact compilation, optimization explanation, and exports. It now supports `compileArtifactsFromSource()` and `explainOptimization()`, which is good. 

Move those into:

```txt
api/compile.ts
api/explain.ts
api/options.ts
```

`src/mod.ts` should mostly re-export public API.

Target:

```ts
parseSource(...)
checkSource(...)
compileArtifactsFromSource(...)
explainOptimization(...)
```

should be thin wrappers over phase modules.

---

## 2. Module/import layer

Current import handling qualifies and merges imported declarations, and now has conservative `pruneImports`.

Move this into:

```txt
module/imports.ts
module/qualify.ts
module/prune.ts
module/graph.ts
```

Main goal:

```txt
import graph resolution
qualification
conservative pruning
module summaries
```

should be separate from API and checker.

Long-term, this becomes the place where you can stop fully merging imported source into one giant program.

---

## 3. Type system layer

Right now type strings still flow through much of the compiler, but refined scalar domains are already strong and central. `refined_scalar.ts` now supports canonical domain operations and interval merging.

Create:

```txt
types/refined_scalar.ts
types/literal_types.ts
types/type_eval.ts
types/type_subst.ts
types/effects.ts
```

The first goal is not full `TypeId` conversion. The first goal is to make type-related functions stop living inside the checker/backend.

Medium-term target:

```ts
type TypeId = number;
type DomainId = number;
```

but only after extraction stabilizes.

---

## 4. Checker layer

`checkProgramInternal` currently performs many phase-like operations in one pipeline: lower do-expressions, group clauses, evaluate types, evaluate consts, resolve members, run specialization passes, lower operators/collectors/constructors, and check functions. 

Split it into:

```txt
check/check_program.ts
check/check_fn.ts
check/check_expr.ts
check/check_pattern.ts
check/check_collections.ts
check/check_constructors.ts
check/check_effects.ts
```

Then `check_program.ts` should read like:

```ts
export function checkProgram(program, options) {
  const ctx = createCheckContext(program, options);

  runPrecheckNormalizers(ctx);
  evaluateTypes(ctx);
  evaluateConsts(ctx);
  specializeProgram(ctx);
  lowerSurfaceSugar(ctx);
  checkDeclarations(ctx);

  return buildCheckResult(ctx);
}
```

The checker should orchestrate. It should not contain all details.

---

## 5. Specialization layer

Specialization is one of the biggest maintenance risks because it creates generated functions, rewrites calls, and affects compile-time scaling. The current pipeline runs inferred and const-param specialization multiple times. 

Move to:

```txt
specialize/infer_type_args.ts
specialize/const_params.ts
specialize/attached_members.ts
specialize/operators.ts
specialize/collectors.ts
specialize/cache.ts
```

Primary goals:

```txt
one specialization context
explicit cache stats
worklist instead of repeated full-program scans
generated function ownership metadata
```

Every generated function should carry:

```ts
generatedBy: "const_param" | "inferred_type" | "clause" | "collector" | ...
sourceFunction: string
specializationKey: string
```

This will make debugging and pruning much easier.

---

## 6. Recurrence layer

The repo now documents recurrence analysis as a compiler feature. Recurrence summaries classify recursive functions as finite static, tail-linear, structural, or general. 

Move recurrence-specific code out of `optimize.ts`:

```txt
recurrence/analyze.ts
recurrence/classify.ts
recurrence/finite_unfold.ts
recurrence/clause_dispatch.ts
recurrence/tail_group_lower.ts
```

This phase should own:

```txt
domain-refined recursive clauses
finite static unfolding
large finite recursion -> loop-compatible lowering
tail-recursive group normalization
```

This keeps recursion-first language design from being scattered across checker, optimizer, and backend.

---

## 7. Facts layer

The optimization system should become fact-driven.

Create:

```txt
facts/abstract_values.ts
facts/call_graph.ts
facts/effect_facts.ts
facts/layout_facts.ts
facts/domain_facts.ts
facts/cost.ts
```

These modules should not rewrite the program. They only compute facts.

Example:

```ts
collectFunctionFacts(program): Map<FnId, FunctionFacts>
collectRecurrenceFacts(program): Map<FnId, Recurrence>
collectLayoutFacts(program): Map<FnId, LayoutFacts>
collectCallGraph(program): CallGraph
```

Then optimizer and backend consume facts.

---

## 8. Optimization layer

`optimize.ts` now contains profiles, plans, summaries, recurrence handling, abstract folding, inlining, local cleanup, and rule IDs.

Split into:

```txt
opt/profiles.ts
opt/plan.ts
opt/rules.ts
opt/apply.ts
opt/inline.ts
opt/local_cleanup.ts
opt/dce.ts
```

The plan should become the heart of the optimizer:

```txt
facts -> plan -> apply high-level actions -> local cleanup
```

Avoid letting each pass rediscover the same decisions.

---

## 9. Layout layer

The backend currently owns much of the layout planning. It now exposes `summarizeBackendLayoutDecisions()`, which is good, but that means layout planning is still backend-coupled. 

Move planning to:

```txt
layout/flatten.ts
layout/fixed_array_plan.ts
layout/packed.ts
layout/scratch.ts
layout/local_slots.ts
layout/products.ts
```

Backend lowering should consume a `LayoutPlan`.

Target:

```ts
const layoutPlan = planLayouts(program, facts, profile);
const backend = lowerProgram(program, layoutPlan, options);
```

This makes layout decisions testable before WAT generation.

---

## 10. Backend and Wasm split

`backend.ts` currently handles backend planning, lowering, cleanup, WAT, Wasm, memory models, branch heap, SIMD, and layout decisions. 

Split into:

```txt
backend/lower_module.ts
backend/lower_fn.ts
backend/lower_expr.ts
backend/lower_tail_loop.ts
backend/lower_match.ts
backend/lower_arrays.ts
backend/lower_branch_heap.ts
backend/instr.ts
backend/cleanup.ts

wasm/wat.ts
wasm/binary.ts
wasm/sections.ts
wasm/names.ts
wasm/branch_hints.ts
```

Backend should output a backend IR/module.

Wasm should only encode/render.

---

# Main architectural rule

Every phase should obey this:

```txt
Input data + facts + profile -> output data + diagnostics + trace
```

Avoid:

```txt
implicit global mutation
hidden generated declarations
backend-only knowledge
name-based prelude special cases
```

The docs already say optimization eligibility should be structural, not based on `prelude.*` names. 

---

# Migration plan

## Milestone 1: Extract without behavior changes

Goal: reduce file size and improve navigation without changing semantics.

Extract from `mod.ts`:

```txt
module/imports.ts
module/qualify.ts
module/prune.ts
api/compile.ts
api/explain.ts
```

Acceptance:

```txt
all tests pass
compileArtifactsFromSource unchanged
explainOptimization unchanged
pruneImports unchanged
```

---

## Milestone 2: Extract optimization plan modules

Move from `optimize.ts`:

```txt
opt/profiles.ts
opt/plan.ts
opt/rules.ts
facts/abstract_values.ts
recurrence/analyze.ts
```

Acceptance:

```txt
summarizeOptimizationPlan output unchanged
summarizeRecurrences output unchanged
benchmark WAT shape unchanged
```

---

## Milestone 3: Extract specialization modules

Move specialization and generated-function logic out of `check.ts`.

Target files:

```txt
specialize/infer_type_args.ts
specialize/const_params.ts
specialize/cache.ts
specialize/attached_members.ts
```

Acceptance:

```txt
same generated functions
same diagnostics
specialization cache counters available
bench_const_params still reproduces current behavior
```

This milestone is where compile-time scaling work becomes much easier.

---

## Milestone 4: Extract backend layout planning

Move layout planning from backend into `layout/`.

Acceptance:

```txt
summarizeBackendLayoutDecisions becomes summarizeLayoutPlan
backend consumes LayoutPlan
WAT/Wasm unchanged
layout plan tests pass
```

---

## Milestone 5: Split backend lowering and Wasm encoding

Move WAT/Wasm-specific code out of backend lowering.

Acceptance:

```txt
emitWat unchanged
emitWasm unchanged
branch hint section unchanged
name section behavior unchanged
```

---

## Milestone 6: Introduce stable phase tracing

Every phase should optionally return:

```ts
interface PhaseTrace {
  phase: string;
  ms: number;
  inputCounts: Record<string, number>;
  outputCounts: Record<string, number>;
  decisions?: OptimizationDecision[];
}
```

Acceptance:

```txt
compileArtifactsFromSource can report parse/import/check/opt/layout/backend/wasm subphases
benchmarks can show where compile time went
```

---

# Recommended final structure of tests

```txt
tests/
  parser/
  checker/
  type_functions/
  refined_domains/
  specialization/
  recurrence/
  optimization_plan/
  layout/
  backend/
  wasm/
  integration/
  benchmarks/
```

Important new tests:

```txt
optimization_plan/prelude_equivalence_test.ts
optimization_plan/rule_decision_test.ts
specialization/scaling_test.ts
module/prune_imports_test.ts
layout/layout_plan_test.ts
recurrence/domain_recursion_test.ts
```

For every major optimization, test both:

```txt
plan decision
final WAT shape
```

Example:

```txt
Plan: recurrence.lower.tail_loop
WAT: contains loop, no recursive call
```

---

# Code quality rules

## 1. No new giant phase files

Any file over roughly:

```txt
1000 lines
```

should be split unless it is generated code or a flat data table.

## 2. No optimizer rule without a rule ID

Every optimization should have:

```txt
rule id
structural matcher
reason string
plan decision if high-level
test
```

## 3. No name-based prelude optimizations

Allowed:

```txt
structural fixed-array update
structural tail recursion
structural product projection
structural refined-domain branch
```

Not allowed:

```txt
if name === "prelude.array_static.RangeIter.fold"
```

## 4. Generated declarations must carry provenance

Generated declarations should record:

```ts
generatedBy
sourceName
specializationKey
```

That will make debugging, pruning, and plan explanations much easier.

## 5. Prefer summaries over rescans

If a phase needs:

```txt
call graph
effect facts
recurrence facts
layout facts
```

it should consume the summary from `facts/`, not rescan the entire AST independently.


